    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1197">

                <pb facs="1400" n="1202" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1202"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">J. C. S.
                    Files</note>
                <head>No. 1197<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the United States Chiefs of
                        Staff</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d1197-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        C. C. S. 891/1</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-19">19 July 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Combined Chiefs of Staff
                        Machinery After the War With Japan</hi></p>
                <p>With reference to C. C. S. 891,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d1197-f2"/> the political relationship of the United States with
                    other nations in the period following this war
                    is not yet sufficiently defined to permit the United States Chiefs of Staff to
                    discuss at this date the post-war relationships between the respective military
                    staffs.</p>
                <p>The United States Chiefs of Staff will bring up for consideration the problem of
                    the most effective military machinery to be used from now forward and prior to
                    the end of the Japanese war.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d1197-f3"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1197-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1197-f1-content">
                <p>Noted by the Combined Chiefs of Staff at their 196th Meeting, July 19. See <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg113">p. 113</ref>. Cf. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg80">p. 80</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1197-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1197-f2-content">
                <p><ref target="frus1945Berlinv01#d550">Document No. 550, printed in vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi></ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1197-f3" n="3" xml:id="d1197-f3-content">
                <p>This paragraph refers to item 5, paragraph <hi rendition="#italic">e</hi>, of the
                    minutes of the 195th Meeting of the Combined Chiefs of Staff, July 18. See <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg86">pp. 86</ref>, <ref
                        target="#pg113">113</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
